<!--
  TAOM war-elephant Monster — READY-TO-DROP reference (authored 2026-06-05).

  Integration: copy this file to
    <game>/Modules/LOTRLOME_Armory/ModuleData/Monsters/LOTR/lotr_monster_elephant.xml
  then register it in LOTRLOME_Armory/SubModule.xml next to the spider's registration, e.g.:
    <XmlNode><XmlName id="Monsters" path="Monsters/LOTR/lotr_monster_elephant"/>
      <IncludedGameTypes><GameType value="Campaign"/><GameType value="CampaignStoryMode"/><GameType value="CustomGame"/></IncludedGameTypes>
    </XmlNode>

  This is a 1-for-1 of the upstream beasts pack's elephant Monster (decompiled 2026-06-05) with:
    - id  : elephant -> taom_war_elephant   (MUST match Main/Features/Elephant/ElephantConfig.ElephantMonsterId)
    - the bone block kept verbatim — these names match our imported `elephant_skeleton` (verified bone-for-bone).

  ⚠️ TWO 1.4.5 SEAMS (the upstream pack's are 1.2.12 — do NOT reuse them):
    - action_set="as_war_elephant"   — author a v1.4.5 action-set bound to `elephant_skeleton` with TAOM-compiled
                                        clips (act_war_elephant_walk/idle/turn/.../attack_1..3). NOT the upstream pack's as_elephant.
    - monster_usage="war_elephant"   — author a v1.4.5 monster_usage_set (use a vanilla quadruped-mount usage as the
                                        template). NOT the upstream pack's `elephant` usage.
  Until those exist the elephant spawns as a mount but won't animate; the C# trample DAMAGE still works
  (act_war_elephant_attack_* resolve to act_none gracefully).
-->
<Monsters>
	<Monster
		id="taom_war_elephant"
		action_set="as_war_elephant"
